# THIS IS A PUBLIC REPOSITORY. Everything committed here is permanent.
#
# Deleting a public repo later does NOT retrieve it - forks, caches and archives persist. So this
# file is a deny-list written BEFORE any content, and the rule for this repo is:
#
#     NEVER run `git add .` here. Add named files only.
#
# The verifier's source code lives in a SEPARATE PRIVATE repository and must never appear here.

# ---- the product. Never publish. ------------------------------------------------------------
gmc_ea_verdict.py
gmc_doctor.py
gmc_*.py
*.mq5
*.ex5
*.ex4

# ---- account and money data -----------------------------------------------------------------
track_record.jsonl
*_report.htm
*_report.html

# EXPLICIT, AUDITED EXCEPTION - added 2026-10-08, and deliberately NOT done with `git add -f`.
# A forced add leaves no record of the decision; this line does.
#
# These two are MY OWN EA's Strategy Tester reports, published so that every figure in
# examples/sample-report.md can be checked end to end instead of believed. Scanned before
# staging: NO account number, NO email address, NO credential - only the demo server name.
#
# They DO contain the EA's full input list, i.e. my strategy's settings. That is accepted: the
# EA failed its own pre-registered bar, so the settings are not worth protecting, and full
# auditability is worth more than hiding a losing configuration.
#
# ANY OTHER REPORT STAYS BLOCKED. A client's report must never appear here under any
# circumstances - see PRIVACY_AND_DISCLOSURE.md.
!examples/be10new_IS_report.htm
!examples/be10new_OOS_report.htm
gmc_expected.json
gmc_locks.json
demo_daily_state.json
manifest.json

